    "topic": "which way toilet paper should hang",
    "summary": "Seth Wheeler's 1891 US patent 465,588 for a perforated toilet-paper roll shows the paper hanging over the front of the roll. In various surveys around 70% prefer 'over'. A 1977 Ann Landers column on the question drew, she said, 15,000 letters. Oprah Winfrey says she is 'an over girl'. 'Under' is said to look tidier and stop cats or toddlers unrolling it.",
    "angle": "The man who patented the roll drew it hanging over.",
